   "firstViewTextSample": "Eden\nFeatures\nMarketplace\nReferral program\nComparisons\nAgencies\nPricing\nDownload\nHelp\nSign in\nStart free\nThe content brain for creators and marketers\nFinally, one place to research viral posts, create original content, sell digital products, grow your email list.\nFinally, one place to\ncreate original conten\n\nSave anything, research millions of posts, schedule everywhere, and run your whole store and email list in one place.\n\nGet started free\nFree includes 50 AI credits. No card. No deadline.\nNew\nLibrary\nDiscover\nCustom AI\nPublish\nChats\nPlan this week's content\n1d\nDevelop newsletter idea\n1d\nOutline a YouTube video\n1d\nFind 10 fresh angles\n3d\nRepurpose my latest essay\n3d\nMore\nBoards\nFavorite Ideas\nYouTube Swipe File\nWriting Inspiration\nAudience Research\nBook Notes\nMy Newsletters\nActive Projects\nDan Koe\nintermittent fasting\n6 platforms\n· Last 6 months · 5× · Top 10%\nDiscover\nCreators\nLists\nAll\nProductivity\nSelf-improvement\nAdd\nBreakouts\nHidden gems\nViral now\nAll-time greats\nAlex Hormozi\n@alexhormozi\n1y\n\nThe single greatest skill you can develop is the ability to stay in a great mood in the absence of things to be in a great mood about.\n\n101K\n17K\n25×\nTop 1%\nJustin Welsh\n@thejustinwelsh\n1mo\n\nThe people who win with AI are not the ones who generate the most. They're the ones who develop the clearest taste.\n\n1.1K\n39\n7.26×\nCodie Sanchez\n418K\n24×\n\nCodie Sanchez The boring business hiding in plain sight\n\n10:38\nHow I Got My Attention Span Back.\nLilla Björn Stationery\n451K views\n28×\nTop 3",
